---
import SiteLayout from "@/layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import Career from "@/components/Career.astro";
import { TAGLINE } from "@/data/site";
---

<SiteLayout title="About · Ryan Saxe" description={TAGLINE} section="about">
  <h1 class="vh">About</h1>
  <div class="about">
    <Career />
    <section class="bio" aria-labelledby="bio-h">
      <h2 id="bio-h" class="vh">Introduction</h2>
      <div class="parts">
        <section>
          <h3>Leading</h3>
          <p>
            Being a builder is central to how I lead. I still write code, design
            models, and spend time in the details. Knowing the work deeply helps
            me see where to take it, make difficult calls, and earn the confidence
            of the people doing it with me.
          </p>
          <p>
            Teaching is a big part of that, too. I love the moment when something
            clicks for someone and they can do something they couldn’t before. I
            want to help people develop the understanding and judgment to find
            their own way through hard problems. That includes having good reasons
            to disagree with me.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h3>Building</h3>
          <p>
            I tend to get absorbed in the things I build. I want to pick apart the
            problem, live in the data, and learn from the people who know the
            business. That understanding shapes everything from how I represent a
            problem in a model to what I decide is worth building.
          </p>
          <p>
            I usually start with a question: what will someone do differently if
            this works? The answer helps me work backward to what the system needs
            to do and how we should measure it. Making that connection can be
            surprisingly hard. But when the measure stays close to the decision,
            improving the system is more likely to improve something people care
            about.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  /* The card switches to one column when the page is narrow. */
  .about {
    container: about / inline-size;
    padding: 0 var(--g);
  }
  /* beside the header's card, the profile card's top lines up with it, and the cards grow no wider than 1216px */
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .about {
      margin-top: -14px;
      padding-left: var(--g-left);
      max-width: calc(var(--g-left) + 1216px + var(--g));
    }
  }
  /*
   * The introduction is a second card under the profile, the same width: two parts side by side, split
   * by a hairline, each under a small label. The profile above already lists every role, so the parts
   * say what the list can't: what Ryan has led, and what he builds.
   */
  .bio {
    margin-top: 20px;
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: var(--card);
    box-shadow: var(--card-shadow);
  }
  .parts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }
  .parts section {
    padding: 30px 40px 34px;
  }
  .parts section:nth-child(odd) {
    border-right: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .parts section:nth-child(n + 3) {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .parts h3 {
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 18px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .parts p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 25px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  @container about (max-width: 760px) {
    .bio {
      margin-top: 14px;
    }
    .parts {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    .parts section {
      padding: 22px 20px 24px;
    }
    .parts section:nth-child(odd) {
      border-right: 0;
    }
    .parts section + section {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .parts p {
      font-size: 14.5px;
      line-height: 24px;
    }
  }
</style>
